     You can check what the permissions should be by starting
a different character (slashem -u someothername), save that
game, then examine the resulting file.  Another possibility
is that recover put your file in some place other than where
slash'em expects to find it.  Normally that would be in the
"save" subdirectory, but some ports allow the user to override
it via config file settings; recover doesn't know how to handle
the latter.  (Ordinarily linux isn't one of those ports, but
either slash'em or Ubuntu-specific customizations might have
changed that.)



